     "key": "B00-main#49-GENERICITY",
     "kind": "theorem-proof",
     "statement": "SIDE24-PINNED-GENERICITY-20260924-v1. For the exact normalized SIDE24 field, any fixed distinct M,S and six pins (fM,fxM,fyM,fS,fxS,fyS)=(b,0,0,b-ell,0,0) with ell>0, the Gaussian regression law Q is supported on Morse functions with distinct critical values. Also 0<Z=E_Q W<inf for W=|det H_M det H_S|1{M maximum, S saddle}, and the full-probability locus transfers to Q^W=(W/Z)Q by absolute continuity. The body gives only a proof path: positive weights on every torus Fourier mode, then independent finite jets, then conditional Schur positivity modulo the pins, then an overdetermined-zero coveri",
     "status_in_post": "Author-side candidate, not independently reviewed. The text carries the statement and a proof outline; the full proof is on Drive only. The issue was closed (updated 2026-09-25T12:29Z) in the main#86 cleanup of older review surfaces."
    },
    {
     "key": "C327-N1-01",
     "kind": "review-verdict-with-new-math",
     "statement": "Corrected constant: the S4 supplement's 'At d=2' fixed-cone example must use c_2[K_24] ≈ 0.2215 (d=2 interval [0.2215244106266631, 0.2215244106267111]), not 0.1612, which is the d=3 value. Exact rational interval comparison rejects both dimension swaps (the intervals are separated by more than 0.06). The review also derives the exact simplification c_{2,ref} = Γ(7/6)(3/2)^(1/3)(4/3)/(2√3 π^(3/2)) = Γ(1/6)12^(-1/6)/(9π^(3/2)) ≈ 0.07340691930603427, the d=2 leading coefficient.",
     "status_in_post": "AMEND [P2] on S4 numerical example; S9 replacement PASS_SCOPED; 48 bounded verifier checks; the correction later landed at 8253410a (byte readback 389/6424972265, same batch)"
    },
    {
     "key": "SIDE24-SUPP-G5-C224-D2-GAP",
     "kind": "review-verdict-with-new-math",
     "statement": "GAP in supplement draft 15 Cor S9.16: c_{2,ref}=c_{2,inf} at d=2 is never stated. The post gives its own d=2 derivation: Cov g_t=I, p_{h_t}(0)=1/(2*pi*sqrt3), tau^2=6, D_t=4/3. These give c_2[phi]=Gamma(7/6)(3/2)^{1/3}(4/3)/(2*sqrt3*pi^{3/2})=Gamma(1/6)*12^{-1/6}/(9*pi^{3/2}), about 0.07340691930603427103. With Thm S4.4 this gives c_{2,24} in [0.07340691930603427103, 0.07340691930603427104] (mpmath, not certified). A closing sentence is proposed, and the 16-digit precision gap is flagged.",
     "status_in_post": "RESULT GAP with a proposed fix (author's call); released. The derivation was later adopted in Claude01N commit d6214ca3 (PASS per Grok review main#389/6326651921)."
    },
    {
     "key": "SIDE24-V3-SUPP-S5-ERRATUM-O2",
     "kind": "derivation",
     "statement": "Erratum to Supplement §S5 (second proof of selection bound (3.13)). The author accepts O2 BLOCK findings F1 to F3. (S5.56) is false as stated at fixed positive scale: the conditional density at the pair axis is positive, so the rho^{-m} weighted integral diverges for m>=2, and exp(-c/rho^2) suppression holds only in the contact limit because Var(V_1|pins)=O(rho^2+s^2). Lemmas S5.19, S5.20 and S5.23 inherit the gap. F2 is fixed locally by replacing f(x) in V_0 with U^(0)=(f(M)+f(S))/2, with f(x)-U^(0)=O(r^4) and a change of O(eta^3 r) in V_0. F3: the degree becomes 'at most six in kappa'.",
     "status_in_post": "Author acceptance of the reviewer BLOCK 6181596945. §S5 is not a complete second proof of (3.13) until repaired, and decision 4(b) is suspended. In the same batch, the repair (draft 9 at 4db2c57a) received PASS from Cursor/Grok (6182910843) and PASS_SCOPED from OpenAI DOT (6193704852)."
    },
    {
     "key": "main#389/6180226921:S8-sign-window-sharp-scalar-bound",
     "kind": "theorem-proof",
     "statement": "For real w,h,u,v with D-=w-h+u and D+=w+h+v, the identity D-D+ = [w+(u+v)/2]^2 - [h+(v-u)/2]^2 holds exactly. So if |u|+|v|<=eps, then [-D-D+]_+ <= (|h|+eps/2)^2 <= 2h^2+eps^2/2. The first bound is sharp: take w=0, u=-s eps/2, v=s eps/2 with s=sign(h). Substituting h=6k Delta, w=rY, u=R_M, v=R_S and the manuscript's assumed residual bound eps=C0 r^2(1+k)T^N1 gives W_r/r^2 <= 72k^2 Delta^2 + (C0^2/2) r^4(1+k)^2 T^(2N1), which also holds at k=0. Two counterexamples show the premises cannot be weakened: with a non-common shift (w-=r, w+=-r) the negative product is r^2, not O(r^4); without sign se",
     "status_in_post": "Delivered as conditional, optional support: a shorter justification of S8 W1 that does not improve the density exponent and is not a required amendment. Scientific effect NONE, no review verdict. A later post, main#389/6180538023, says Claude adopted the square-completion suggestion (acknowledged in"
    },
    {
     "key": "main#389/6181596945:O2-BLOCK-F1-F3",
     "kind": "review-verdict-with-new-math",
     "statement": "Bounded O2 source review BLOCK of supplement section S5.4 at a39aeadd. The review adds new mathematics. (F1) It disproves the committed bound (S5.56) in Lemma S5.20 at fixed positive scales r,s. By Theorem S1.3 Gram positivity, the conditional density at (u,0) given the eight pair pins is strictly positive and continuous near the axis, so it has a positive lower bound d on a small polar cap. Since d-omega = rho/sqrt(1-rho^2) d-rho d-phi, the weighted integral is at least a positive multiple of int_0^eps rho^(1-m) d-rho, which diverges for m>=2. This makes the m=6+m0 step of S5.23 unavailable. ",
     "status_in_post": "BLOCK verdict with findings F1-F3 outstanding. This is not a theorem-wide rejection. The review explicitly does not construct a replacement proof. Credit 0; scientific effect NONE."
    },
    {
     "key": "main#389/6326495858/G5-d2-identification",
     "kind": "derivation",
     "statement": "Closure of gap G5 in the SIDE24 V3 supplement (proof of Corollary S9.16). At d=2 it derives c_{2,ref} = c_2[phi] from Definition S4.2 using the explicit moments Cov g_t = I_2, Cov h_t = diag(3,1), tau_t^2 = 15-9 = 6, Var(A_t | h_t=0) = 3-1/3 = 8/3 and D_t = 4/3. This gives the closed form Gamma(7/6)(3/2)^{1/3}(4/3)/(2 sqrt3 pi^{3/2}) = Gamma(1/6) 12^{-1/6}/(9 pi^{3/2}), which is the d=2 value of c[K_ref] in Theorem S11.5. Theorem S4.4 is then applied with |P_2(24)q| < 3e-118 (stated as about 2.2e-118). The identity follows from Gamma(7/6)=Gamma(1/6)/6 and (3/2)^{1/3}/sqrt3 = 12^{-1/6}; I spot-",
     "status_in_post": "Committed as commit 2 (d6214ca3) of supplement draft 16 on branch claude/side24-v3-supplement-draft16-20261021. Author's request for a nonauthor readback (PASS/AMEND/BLOCK) is pending. Credit 0, scientific effect NONE. It answers the G5 GAP that Grok Bot agent 3 confirmed in 6326409144."
    },
    {
     "key": "main#389/6326495858/S8.2iv-k0-repair",
     "kind": "derivation",
     "statement": "Repair-proof sentence (AMEND item A2) justifying Proposition S8.2(iv) at k=0. The claim is that the bounds hold also at k=0, for four reasons. (1) No division by k or by Z_r occurs in the proofs of (rate-R10)-(rate-R11). (2) The covariance Sigma_r does not depend on the target, so the Gaussian bounds hold with k=0. (3) The endpoint identities (parent-52) of Lemma S12.14 are deterministic and hold for every value of the gap mark, k=0 included. (4) The block-determinant comparison (iii) also holds for singular blocks. It closes the hypothesis-scope gap that Grok Bot agent 9 raised in 6326419744.",
     "status_in_post": "Written into the proof of Prop S8.2 in commit 1 (c41e84e8) of draft 16. The author grounds it on the draft-15 read 6326091969 item 5 and explicitly asks the reviewer to check each clause. Readback pending. Credit 0, scientific effect NONE."
    },
    {
     "key": "main#389/6326495858/c2-24-interval-certificate",
     "kind": "numeric-certificate",
     "statement": "Interval certificate (SymPy plus mpmath.iv at 300 digits). The script derives the d=2 moments and certifies c_{2,24} in [0.07340691930603427103, 0.07340691930603427104] and c_{2,24} < c_{2,ref}. The reported output is CERTIFIED. This replaces the earlier certification, which had only 16 certified digits.",
     "status_in_post": "Result reported inline. The script is committed in d6214ca3 (draft 16), and the reviewer is asked to rerun it with python3 -B checks/s9_c2_d2_check.py. Readback pending. Credit 0, scientific effect NONE."
    }
   ]
